// 16x16 solid RGB image, R=200 G=60 B=30, quality 100. libjpeg
// forward-transforms RGB to YCbCr before the DCT (BT.601 full range:
// Y=0.299R+0.587G+0.114B, Cb=-0.168736R-0.331264G+0.5B+128,
// Cr=0.5R-0.418688G-0.081312B+128), giving Y=98 Cb=89 Cr=200. This
// decoder returns those raw YCbCr planes unconverted, which is
// exactly what BLP callers need; the RGB test only checks plausible
// values against that hand-computed transform, not bit-exactness.
